<title>ROMANIA: Bucharest bourse to extend trading sessions.</title>
<headline>Bucharest bourse to extend trading sessions.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bucharest stock exchange said on Friday it would extend trading next month to five sessions per week instead of three.</p>
<p>The bourse will hold trading sessions from Monday to Friday starting on May 5, a statement said. It said daily trading would be from 9.15 a.m. to 1.30 p.m. (0615 to 1030 GMT).</p>
<p>Next week, the bourse would trade only on Tuesday and Wednesday and would be closed on Thursday, when Romania celebrates Labour Day, the statement said.</p>
<p>The Bucharest stock exchange trades 34 stocks, of which four are listed on the first tier.</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
